sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client1
    participant Client2
    participant Auth as Authorization Service
    participant DB as Auth DB

    Note over Client1,Client2: Same account, same or competing requests arrive nearly simultaneously

    Client1->>Auth: POST /authorizations\nIdempotency-Key=abc123\namount=80
    Client2->>Auth: POST /authorizations\nIdempotency-Key=abc123\namount=80

    par Request 1
        Auth->>DB: Check idempotency key
        DB-->>Auth: Not found
        Auth->>DB: Load account(version=5, available=100)
        DB-->>Auth: Account returned
        Auth->>DB: Reserve funds + insert auth + save idempotency key
        DB-->>Auth: Commit success, version becomes 6
        Auth-->>Client1: 201 AUTHORIZED
    and Request 2
        Auth->>DB: Check idempotency key
        alt Duplicate detected after request 1 commits
            DB-->>Auth: Existing idempotent result found
            Auth-->>Client2: 200 Return same authorization result
        else Concurrent race before request 1 commits
            DB-->>Auth: Not found
            Auth->>DB: Load account(version=5, available=100)
            DB-->>Auth: Account returned
            Auth->>DB: Attempt reserve funds with optimistic locking
            DB-->>Auth: Optimistic lock conflict / unique key conflict
            Auth->>DB: Re-read idempotency key or authorization
            DB-->>Auth: Existing authorization found
            Auth-->>Client2: 200 Return same authorization result
        end
    end